+I migrated the template syntax from Jinja2 to Mako by replacing Jinja-style `{{ ... }}` expressions and `{% ... %}` control blocks with Mako’s `${...}` expressions and `%` control lines. The template logic and output structure were kept the same.

+

+```python

+"""${name}.

+

+% for p in params:

+:param ${p.argument}:

+% if p.annotation:

+:type ${p.argument}: ${p.annotation}

+% endif

+% endfor

+% if return_type:

+:rtype: ${return_type}

+% endif

+"""

+```
